    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d614-a5">

                <pb facs="0715" n="619" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg619"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Mataafa.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Apia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1899-05-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 19,
                    1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We have received your letters of the 17th
                    and 18th of this month, in which you inform us that you will call on us with
                    four high chiefs and a secretary on Saturday next on board our ship the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Badger.</hi></p>
                <p>We shall be pleased to receive you at 9 o’clock in the morning. Three men of war
                    boats of the three powers, each bearing its flag, will arrive at Malie at 7
                    o’clock to escort you to our ship and bring you back.</p>
                <p>We are, sir, yours faithfully,</p>
                <closer>[Signed by each commissioner.]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
